method:
(agreed shape, 2026-10-26; replaces the library's hand-box means and the superframe's
first-step ΔE, which included clipped paper):
- source: the BugNews save, image 3 (1200 x 851);
- sheets: the superframe's four sheet boxes (read from a b* map); each pixel's depth is the number of
  boxes covering it; pixels within 8 px of any sheet edge are dropped (JPEG ringing);
- per depth: the median sRGB of the remaining pixels, converted to CIE L*a*b* (D65, proper sRGB
  linearisation, not 8-bit OpenCV Lab);
- the paper is clipped at white in this save, so depth 0 is reported but every fit and step ratio
  uses depths 1 to 4 only (the unclipped regions);
- fits on depths 1 to 4: L* against depth (linear) and against ln(depth) (Weber-Fechner).
It measures a printed reproduction: it calibrates how the print renders perceived steps.
